.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-HELP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-help
.Nd the operator's command reference and worked recipes, by topic
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar topic | Cm recipes | Cm all
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no argument,
.Nm
prints the topics, the five commands to know first, and the web
console's addresses.
With a topic it prints that topic with examples to copy:
.Bl -tag -width "observability" -compact
.It Cm status
what is running and healthy, and where to look
.It Cm storage
pools, datasets, snapshots
.It Cm vms
making, cloning, snapshotting, listing and deleting virtual machines
.It Cm k8s
a Kubernetes cluster: build, scale, status, reset
.It Cm klab
the multi-distribution test lab
.It Cm replication
ZFS send and receive, locally and between hosts
.It Cm export
virtual machines as disk images, or to AWS
.It Cm backup
snapshots, boot environments, recovery
.It Cm ai
local models, Open WebUI, freeing the GPU
.It Cm observability
Grafana, Hubble, Tetragon
.It Cm cockpit
the console's F-keys
.It Cm firstboot
what runs unattended at first boot, and its logs
.It Cm recipes
end-to-end workflows
.It Cm all
every topic, for a pager or
.Xr grep 1 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The console's keys; output left out here, since it is the list above
in full:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-help cockpit
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-console 8 ,
.Xr kldload-overview 8 ,
.Xr kst 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: the
.Cm ai
topic taught five commands that no longer exist, and the
.Cm cockpit
topic's F-key map was the one from before May.
